WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.249
A laptop provides portability, while a desktop offers easier expansion and larger displays.

00:00:05.249 --> 00:00:09.210
A mini PC can serve as a compact dedicated station.

00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:13.963
A virtual machine can separate research software and files from the host,

00:00:13.963 --> 00:00:18.319
but it still depends on host security, storage, and disciplined configuration.

00:00:18.319 --> 00:00:22.280
Windows, Linux, and macOS can all support responsible OSINT work.

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:27.429
The best choice is the platform the organization can secure, patch, back up,

00:00:27.429 --> 00:00:28.221
and support.

00:00:28.221 --> 00:00:32.182
Specialized appearance or unfamiliar complexity does not create better intelligence.

00:00:32.182 --> 00:00:36.539
Memory requirements depend on browser tabs, local document processing, mapping, spreadsheets,

00:00:36.539 --> 00:00:39.311
virtual machines, and approved local AI tools.

00:00:39.311 --> 00:00:42.480
Sufficient memory prevents constant swapping and unstable multitasking.

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:48.025
Storage should use dependable solid-state media with capacity for active cases and recovery operations.

00:00:48.025 --> 00:00:51.985
A second display can improve note taking and source comparison,

00:00:51.985 --> 00:00:55.154
but screen privacy and physical workspace design matter.

00:00:55.154 --> 00:01:01.095
Portable systems may need privacy filters or careful placement when sensitive case material is visible.

00:01:01.095 --> 00:01:05.452
Virtual machines are useful for snapshots, reproducible environments, and tool separation.

00:01:05.452 --> 00:01:09.016
Snapshots are not backups, and isolation is not absolute.

00:01:09.016 --> 00:01:12.581
Keep the host, hypervisor, guest system, and browsers updated,

00:01:12.581 --> 00:01:17.334
and understand where copied files, shared folders, and clipboard data are stored.

00:01:17.334 --> 00:01:18.522
Select practical reliability.

00:01:18.522 --> 00:01:22.879
Use supported hardware, tested encryption, known recovery methods, and documented peripherals.

00:01:22.879 --> 00:01:28.820
Build enough headroom for normal workloads without buying complexity that cannot be maintained or audited.
